  "_comment": "Section registry for site/oracle (the single source of section order, numbering, titles, module staleness and deck inclusion). The page numbers sections, figures, tables and cross-references from this list at render time (app.js numberSections); present.js titles its pages from it; validate-data.mjs fails when a cross-reference (ref('id') in app.js / present.js, data-ref in index.html, {{sec:id}} in the JSON narrative) names an id that is not here. Never type a section number anywhere else. `modules` lists the data files that feed the section (keys of freshness.modules), so every chart footer can show the period end, the ET refresh time and a stale flag of the right module. `deck` = the board presentation builds a page for it; `deck_order` = the order of the deck pages (the page follows the story order below; the deck keeps the board order). `group: reference` = the section lives in the collapsed Reference appendix and is numbered R1, R2… `label_*` = a label shown instead of a number (the Summary is 'Start here'). `path` = which reading paths open the section by default (5 = five minutes, 20 = twenty minutes; the full path opens everything).",
